// Pull request: #6122 update: Regsvr32 detection rules tuning and expansion
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6122
// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potentially Suspicious Regsvr32 Remote Pattern
// Sigma ID: 867356ee-9352-41c9-a8f2-1be690d78216
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-24 | Modified: 2026-10-18
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.010
// Description: Detects regsvr32 execution to load/register DLLs from remote locations via HTTP, HTTPS, or FTP
//   protocols. This is a common technique used by attackers to bypass application whitelisting and
//   execute malicious code.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/mrd0x/status/1461041276514623491
//   - https://twitter.com/tccontre18/status/1480950986650832903
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Regsvr32/
//   - https://www.cyberproof.com/blog/beyond-powershell-analyzing-the-multi-action-clickfix-variant/
//   - https://github.com/SuperKieran/WooyunDrops/blob/gh-pages/static/drops/1161.Use%20SCT%20to%20Bypass%20Application%20Whitelisting%20Protection.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/fba4b94a2237d0ec8fe1cd5dc9c4c29dc6d3e4c4/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_regsvr32_remote_pattern.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "REGSVR32.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -i" or ProcessCommandLine contains " /i" or ProcessCommandLine contains " –i" or ProcessCommandLine contains " —i" or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―i" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -s" or ProcessCommandLine contains " /s" or ProcessCommandLine contains " –s" or ProcessCommandLine contains " —s" or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―s") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "ftp://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://")
